WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.270 --> 00:00:01.889
- Do you want your house back?

00:00:01.889 --> 00:00:02.912
- [Protesters] Yeah!

00:00:02.912 --> 00:00:03.745
- Take it!

00:00:03.745 --> 00:00:05.730
- [Rioter] He's breaking the window.

00:00:05.730 --> 00:00:07.660
- [Rioter] Get in.

00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.700
- [Reporter] A violent mob
attacked the US Capitol

00:00:09.700 --> 00:00:11.870
on January 6th and disrupted the vote

00:00:11.870 --> 00:00:14.540
to certify the 2020 presidential election

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.023
after President Trump
urged them on at a rally.

00:00:18.363 --> 00:00:21.970
- [Officer] MPD JOCC to Capitol
Command, just advising you

00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:25.900
that the MPD has declared
this a breach of the Capitol

00:00:25.900 --> 00:00:27.673
as well as a riot at the Capitol.

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:30.860
- [Reporter] A Capitol
Police officer was killed

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.120
and four rioters died in the chaos,

00:00:33.120 --> 00:00:35.072
one shot by Capitol Police.

00:00:35.072 --> 00:00:37.980
- [Rioters] USA, USA, USA!

00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:39.520
- [Reporter] The Wall Street
Journal analyzed hours

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:41.440
of video footage of the pro-Trump mob

00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:44.570
as well as emergency responder
scanner audio from the riot

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:47.260
and spoke to security experts
including a former Head

00:00:47.260 --> 00:00:49.210
of the Capitol Police, Terrance Gainer,

00:00:49.210 --> 00:00:52.350
to better understand how a mob
of thousands overran police

00:00:52.350 --> 00:00:54.500
and attacked the nation's Capitol,

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.540
- [Officer] Back up!

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:56.490
- [Reporter] Threatening the safety

00:00:56.490 --> 00:00:59.290
of the highest ranking officials
in American government.

00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.050
The Journal found that the Capitol Police

00:01:03.050 --> 00:01:05.890
failed both strategically
and operationally

00:01:05.890 --> 00:01:07.040
to secure the building.

00:01:08.970 --> 00:01:12.030
Capitol Police and DC Metropolitan
Police did not respond

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:13.700
to multiple requests for comment.

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:15.640
In a previous statement,
the Capitol Police said

00:01:15.640 --> 00:01:18.623
its officers were heroic given
the situation they faced.

00:01:20.169 --> 00:01:21.002
- [Rioter] You traitor!

00:01:21.002 --> 00:01:23.400
- [Reporter] Their Union said
the officers lacked backup

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.683
and equipment to control the protesters.

00:01:26.764 --> 00:01:30.330
(sirens wailing)

00:01:30.330 --> 00:01:31.840
It began at a rally

00:01:31.840 --> 00:01:34.380
challenging the Presidential
election results.

00:01:34.380 --> 00:01:37.230
- And we fight, we fight like hell.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:38.950
And if you don't fight like hell,

00:01:38.950 --> 00:01:40.950
you're not gonna have a country anymore.

00:01:42.290 --> 00:01:43.770
- [Reporter] By around 12:20 PM,

00:01:43.770 --> 00:01:46.190
hundreds of raucous protesters
were making their way

00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:47.380
to the Capitol.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.200
While some headed for the east side,

00:01:49.200 --> 00:01:51.880
the majority approached
directly from the west.

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.910
At 12:52, the protesters encounter

00:01:53.910 --> 00:01:55.270
their first police presence

00:01:55.270 --> 00:01:57.120
on the northwest side of the Capitol.

00:01:59.284 --> 00:02:01.034
- [Rioters] Let's go!

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.790
- [Reporter] We can see only
eight Capitol Police officers,

00:02:04.790 --> 00:02:06.580
none are in riot gear.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:09.360
They're standing behind a
temporary metal barrier.

00:02:09.360 --> 00:02:11.006
- [Rioter] We pay your bills.

00:02:11.006 --> 00:02:13.183
You back the (beeping) off!

00:02:13.183 --> 00:02:14.470
You back off!

00:02:14.470 --> 00:02:16.440
- [Reporter] This type of
movable barrier is meant

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:18.410
to signal that an area is off limits,

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.659
not to stop a wave of violent protesters.

00:02:21.659 --> 00:02:23.620
- [Protesters] USA, USA, USA!

00:02:23.620 --> 00:02:26.020
- [Reporter] The protesters
quickly become aggressive

00:02:26.020 --> 00:02:28.260
and easily push through the barriers.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.660
It's clear that Capitol
Police were not prepared

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:31.983
for this type of crowd.

00:02:32.996 --> 00:02:34.596
- [Protester] Oh, (beeping)!

00:02:34.596 --> 00:02:36.846
Whoa, whoa, whoa, hey, hey!

00:02:38.140 --> 00:02:39.370
- [Reporter] The small group of officers

00:02:39.370 --> 00:02:41.773
are quickly overwhelmed
and need to fall back.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:47.550
Capitol Police Chief Steven
Sund who has since resigned

00:02:47.550 --> 00:02:48.820
said in a previous statement

00:02:48.820 --> 00:02:51.500
that officers responded valiantly
when faced with thousands

00:02:51.500 --> 00:02:54.793
of individuals involved in
violent riotous actions.

00:02:56.870 --> 00:02:59.420
The number of rioters is
growing as they rush the base

00:02:59.420 --> 00:03:00.620
of the Capitol building.

00:03:03.240 --> 00:03:05.650
Just a few minutes later by 12:57,

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:07.440
we can see Capitol Police scramble

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:10.620
to form a skirmish line
further up the Capitol stairs

00:03:10.620 --> 00:03:12.190
to prevent any further advance.

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:14.330
- [Protesters] USA, USA, USA!

00:03:14.330 --> 00:03:16.230
- [Reporter] A Capitol Police
Civil Disturbance Unit,

00:03:16.230 --> 00:03:19.250
or CDU, arrives to strengthen the line.

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:21.890
These officers are more
heavily equipped with helmets,

00:03:21.890 --> 00:03:23.805
body armor and batons.

00:03:23.805 --> 00:03:26.080
- We are protesting that this is our home.

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:27.220
- [Reporter] They're also trying to spot

00:03:27.220 --> 00:03:29.803
the most threatening
actors and any ringleaders.

00:03:30.882 --> 00:03:31.983
- [Protesters] We want Trump!

00:03:31.983 --> 00:03:32.816
We want Trump!

00:03:32.816 --> 00:03:34.110
- [Reporter] Visible in the sea of rioters

00:03:34.110 --> 00:03:36.370
are individuals wearing
military-style gear

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:39.690
with Kevlar vests, some have
potential makeshift weaponry

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:41.643
like this bat and these flags,

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.910
and orange-colored tape
and hats that indicate

00:03:44.910 --> 00:03:48.177
that groups may be
coordinating their actions.

00:03:48.177 --> 00:03:49.010
- [Protesters] We want Trump!

00:03:50.690 --> 00:03:52.100
- [Reporter] At 1:10, about 10 minutes

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:55.380
after the CDU arrived,
the violence escalates.

00:03:55.380 --> 00:03:57.723
The mob begins to brawl with the officers.

00:03:59.680 --> 00:04:02.853
Here, a flag is thrown,
hitting an officer in the head.

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:06.820
Experts we spoke to say
another riot platoon

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.670
should have been on the scene by now.

00:04:11.749 --> 00:04:13.410
- [Officer] Move back!
- [Officer] Please, move back.

00:04:13.410 --> 00:04:14.890
- [Reporter] Instead, we can see only

00:04:14.890 --> 00:04:17.010
a DC Metropolitan Police Bike Unit

00:04:17.010 --> 00:04:18.940
has arrived as reinforcement.

00:04:18.940 --> 00:04:20.440
These units are called
because they can get

00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:23.380
into crowded locations quickly
and their helmets, spikes

00:04:23.380 --> 00:04:25.383
and other gear offer some protection.

00:04:27.710 --> 00:04:29.720
Rushing to reestablish the dividing line,

00:04:29.720 --> 00:04:31.520
they deploy pepper spray,

00:04:31.520 --> 00:04:34.160
but some of the mob
counter with bear spray,

00:04:34.160 --> 00:04:35.873
a sign that they expected a fight.

00:04:36.867 --> 00:04:37.810
- [Rioters] Yeah, yeah, yeah!

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.560
- [Officer] Multiple officers injured

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:41.213
at the Capitol, west side.

00:04:42.780 --> 00:04:45.260
- [Reporter] At 1:35, we
see more Metropolitan Police

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.730
on the scene attempting to
aid the Capitol officers

00:04:47.730 --> 00:04:49.650
on the fast weakening line.

00:04:49.650 --> 00:04:50.640
- [Rioter] I'll kill you!

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:53.380
- [Reporter] No more backup
arrives and the officers endure

00:04:53.380 --> 00:04:56.643
over an hour of assault from
the mob, barely holding on.

00:04:58.250 --> 00:05:01.180
At 1:41, we hear police
put out a call that is used

00:05:01.180 --> 00:05:04.180
to signal that a unit
is being overwhelmed.

00:05:04.180 --> 00:05:05.630
- [Officer] Broken arrow.

00:05:05.630 --> 00:05:08.063
- [Officer] Med unit on
citywide with a priority.

00:05:09.110 --> 00:05:10.333
- [Officer] Yeah, they're
coming over in reference

00:05:10.333 --> 00:05:13.662
to the Capitol building, broken arrow.

00:05:13.662 --> 00:05:14.860
- [Rioter] Go, go, go!

00:05:14.860 --> 00:05:16.920
- [Reporter] By 2:28,
more people are breaking

00:05:16.920 --> 00:05:19.600
through the skirmish
line, forcing officers

00:05:19.600 --> 00:05:23.247
to chase them down and
further weakening the line.

00:05:23.247 --> 00:05:24.490
- [Rioter] Cut the line!

00:05:24.490 --> 00:05:26.530
- [Reporter] Then, after
nearly an hour and a half

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:28.820
of hostilities, the last line of defense

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.560
between the rioters and
the lawmakers inside

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.633
finally breaks apart entirely,
sending the scene into chaos.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:40.840
An officer is pushed off a
ledge where just below him,

00:05:40.840 --> 00:05:42.380
a group of officers are pinned

00:05:42.380 --> 00:05:44.710
and assaulted with a fire extinguisher.

00:05:44.710 --> 00:05:46.313
More officers fall back.

00:05:47.702 --> 00:05:48.823
- [Rioter] USA!

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:52.030
- [Reporter] And once the
skirmish line on the west side

00:05:52.030 --> 00:05:55.123
of the Capitol fails, the
mob storms the building.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:59.360
As the scene spirals further
out of control, the mob beats

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:03.653
a fallen officer on the ground
and drags him down the steps.

00:06:04.700 --> 00:06:07.090
An emerging timeline shows
requests and approvals

00:06:07.090 --> 00:06:09.400
for more police help happening too late

00:06:09.400 --> 00:06:11.213
and too slow at every turn.

00:06:12.090 --> 00:06:13.540
- Help!

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:14.810
- [Reporter] Verbal approval to deploy

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.040
the DC National Guard
was not given until 3 PM,

00:06:18.040 --> 00:06:21.050
about 30 minutes after
rioters breached the Capitol.

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:23.083
- [Rioter] Stop, he can't breathe!

00:06:23.083 --> 00:06:24.996
Take his (beeping) mask off,

00:06:24.996 --> 00:06:29.163
he can't (beeping) breathe, dude!

